of Immunopathogenesis and Bioinformatics, Clinical Services Program, SAIC-Frederick, Inc., National Cancer Institute at Frederick, Frederick, MD 21702, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Sherman BT", "lastName": "Sherman", "firstName": "Brad T", "initials": "BT"}, {"fullName": "Lempicki RA", "lastName": "Lempicki", "firstName": "Richard A", "initials": "RA", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7059-409X"}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7059-409X"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["supporting_data", "recommended_reviews"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "1", "volume": "37", "journalIssueId": 1589237, "dateOfPublication": "2009 Jan", "monthOfPublication": 1, "yearOfPublication": 2009, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Nucleic Acids Res", "title": "Nucleic acids research", "essn": "1362-4962", "issn": "0305-1048", "nlmid": "0411011", "isoabbreviation": "Nucleic Acids Res"}, "printPublicationDate": "2009-01-01"}, "pubYear": "2009", "pageInfo": "1-13", "abstractText": "Functional analysis of large gene lists, derived in most cases from emerging high-throughput genomic, proteomic and bioinformatics scanning approaches, is still a challenging and daunting task. The gene-annotation enrichment analysis is a promising high-throughput strategy that increases the likelihood for investigators to identify biological processes most pertinent to their study. Approximately 68 bioinformatics enrichment tools that are currently available in the community are collected in this survey. Tools are uniquely categorized into three major classes, according to their underlying enrichment algorithms. The comprehensive collections, unique tool classifications and associated questions/issues will provide a more comprehensive and up-to-date view regarding the advantages, pitfalls and recent trends in a simpler tool-class level rather than by a tool-by-tool approach. Thus, the survey will help tool designers/developers and experienced end users understand the underlying algorithms and pertinent details of particular tool categories/tools, enabling them to make the best choices for their particular research interests.", "affiliation": "Laboratory of Immunopathogenesis and Bioinformatics, Clinical Services Program, SAIC-Frederick, Inc., National Cancer Institute at Frederick, Frederick, MD 21702, USA.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NCI NIH HHS", "acronym": "CO", "grantId": "N01-CO-56000", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Computational Biology", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "TD", "qualifierName": "trends"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Genes"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Algorithms"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Software", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "CL", "qualifierName": "classification"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "TD", "qualifierName": "trends"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Databases, Genetic"}]}, "subsetList": {"subset": [{"code": "IM", "name": "Index Medicus"}]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "nar.oxfordjournals.org", "url": "http://nar.oxfordjournals.org/cgi/content/full/37/1/1"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "nar.oxfordjournals.org", "url": "http://nar.oxfordjournals.org/cgi/reprint/37/1/1.pdf"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "abs", "site": "nar.oxfordjournals.org", "url": "http://nar.oxfordjournals.org/cgi/content/abstract/37/1/1"}, {"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S